title: "RCC RefCert: A Research Toolkit for Structure-Fair Quantum Circuit Complexity"
type: software
version: 0.3.0
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24248347"
url: "https://github.com/yeruciwenrou-dotcom/rcc-refcert/releases/tag/v0.3.0"
date-released: 2026-11-15
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/yeruciwenrou-dotcom/rcc-refcert"
abstract: >-
  RCC RefCert is a research toolkit for structure-fair quantum circuit
  complexity. Reference-Contingent Complexity (RCC) takes the structure
  supplied by a physical background as the zero point for resource accounting.
  In a fixed admissible model, information from the final state gives a
  rigorous lower bound on the cost of preparing a target to a specified
  accuracy. Researchers can build finite-control models, verify reference
  certificates and calculate these bounds from an exact target spectrum or
  from observed counts for a projection measurement specified in advance.
  For exact diagonal-preserving models, a successful candidate program
  supplies an upper bound on the optimal cost. Numerical matrix models
  report each candidate's cost and distance from the target. Window RCC
  compares subsystem complexity in pure and mixed states and follows local
  and correlation contributions along a preparation. Analysis bundles
  preserve the inputs and results for independent verification.
